[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:A Pretty Carpet]
[00:14.20]What is the writer's carpet made of?
[00:19.68]We have just moved into a new house and I have been working hard all morning.
[00:28.02]I have been trying to get my new room in order.
[00:32.53]This has not been easy because I own over a thousand books.
[00:38.60]To make matters worse,
[00:40.82]the room is rather small,
[00:43.42]so I have temporarily put my books on the floor.
[00:47.63]At the moment, they cover every inch of floor space
[00:52.78]and I actually have to walk on them to get in or out of the room.
[00:58.76]A short while ago, my sister helped me to carry one of my old bookcases up the stairs.
[01:07.36]She went into my room and got a big surprise when she saw all those books on the floor.
[01:15.29]'This is the prettiest carpet I have ever seen,' she said.
[01:20.55]She gazed at it for some time then added,
[01:24.34]'You don't need bookcases at all.
[01:26.73]You can sit here in your spare time and read the carpet!'
